51	 * Gson} instance and then invoking {@link #toJson(Object)} or {@link #fromJson(String, Class)}
52	 * methods on it. {@code Gson} instances are thread-safe so you can reuse them freely across
53	 * multiple threads.
54	 *
55	 * <p>You can create a {@code Gson} instance by invoking {@link #Gson() new Gson()} if the default
56	 * configuration is all you need. You can also use {@link GsonBuilder} to build a {@code Gson}
57	 * instance with various configuration options such as versioning support, pretty printing, and
58	 * custom serialization and deserialization logic.
59	 *
60	 * <p>Gson is based on the concept of {@link TypeAdapter}s which contain the actual logic for
61	 * serializing and deserializing a Java type. For more advanced use cases {@link TypeAdapterFactory}
62	 * can be used which allows inspecting the Java type at runtime and providing a {@code TypeAdapter}
63	 * for it. {@code TypeAdapterFactory} also supports delegating to adapters for other types, which is
64	 * useful when handling types which are themselves composed of multiple types or when extending an
65	 * existing adapter.<br>
66	 * The interfaces {@link JsonSerializer} and {@link JsonDeserializer} allow processing JSON data as
67	 * tree structures; this can make their usage easier than {@code TypeAdapter}, but they are not as
68	 * efficient.
69	 *
70	 * <p>Gson provides built-in type adapters for many standard Java types such as {@code List}, {@code
71	 * Integer} or {@code String}. For unknown classes it uses reflection to inspect the fields of the
72	 * class and uses them for the JSON structure.
73	 *
74	 * <p>When serializing or deserializing a type, {@code Gson} instances cache the {@code TypeAdapter}
75	 * they obtained from a {@code TypeAdapterFactory} for that type. It can therefore improve
76	 * performance to reuse a single {@code Gson} instance (for example by storing it in a {@code static
77	 * final} field), especially when relying on the built-in reflection-based adapter or when using
78	 * custom type adapter factories.
